{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1214 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d9b316f1145d9d984c4b85dd599f18fe3cdeb46c2d9aacc0338ea7bb9214aca7" :edb/db-before-t 1213 :edb/db-after-t 1214 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534526 50 #inst "2026-10-07T20:23:26.810Z" 13194139534526 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293215 13194139534526 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293222 13194139534526 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293204 13194139534526 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293211 13194139534526 true] [17592186101296 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534526 true] [17592186101296 1100 "Find the number $c > 0$ such that the average value of $f(x) = 9 + 8x - 3x^{2}$ on the interval $[0, c]$ is equal to $-3$." 13194139534526 false] [17592186101296 1100 "Find the number $c>0$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9+8x-3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-3.$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186101296 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9+8x-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(9x+4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(9c+4{c}^{2}-{c}^{3})-(0)] \\\\ -3 & =9+4c-{c}^{2} \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c-12 & =0 \\\\ (c+2)(c-6) & =0 \\\\ c & =-2,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=6$ only." 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293205 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1089 "q-30872" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1100 "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1113 #uuid "215232ce-c44e-5876-848b-764311244f79" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293204 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293206 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293207 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293208 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293209 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293210 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1041 "selection" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293210 13194139534526 true] [17592186293205 1110 #uuid "78028f31-056b-5364-8107-f135cf6c2c43" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293206 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293206 1111 #uuid "3e0dc1c3-210c-5bca-a788-1a8e3ae5aa5b" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293207 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293207 1111 #uuid "9e5db305-e741-5c95-b785-661bf4589106" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293208 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293208 1111 #uuid "9ec70a2e-1ad7-5fda-b8de-b5e200aa8ec6" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293209 1034 "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293209 1111 #uuid "02c1490b-2304-57b0-ae21-f557180a5938" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293210 1034 "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293210 1111 #uuid "11239261-2fd4-5af3-89ad-fcad1c9e9621" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293212 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1089 "q-316309" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/assets/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1113 #uuid "b35a20f7-a229-5f61-92db-08090927f688" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293211 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293213 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293214 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1041 "field-1" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293214 13194139534526 true] [17592186293212 1110 #uuid "4ec9cd8e-8d1e-5d0a-964b-6930c346238a" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293213 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293213 1111 #uuid "be6a37d7-62f4-53f8-833b-534cf983c83f" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293214 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293214 1111 #uuid "f9a898a6-66e6-5802-84f6-63fa5a1e03d4" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293216 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1089 "q-3289" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1100 "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1113 #uuid "d52db9f0-626b-5e49-b54e-8b0ef2daded7" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293215 1145 "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293217 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293218 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293219 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293220 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293221 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1041 "selection" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293221 13194139534526 true] [17592186293216 1110 #uuid "96027c73-d970-5a5d-8d9b-19336d1c17a2" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293217 1034 "{61.2}^{∘}F" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293217 1111 #uuid "4fc96793-beac-5813-aa2c-a00493884514" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293218 1034 "{50.0}^{∘}F" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293218 1111 #uuid "4086c4ab-277f-5a4b-80e4-6468e51e9be5" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293219 1034 "{52.1}^{∘}F" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293219 1111 #uuid "879925b4-e44a-5ae1-ba63-3d2d0d84faf9" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293220 1034 "{56.5}^{∘}F" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293220 1111 #uuid "b6cf9b1f-8736-5d0f-a4e0-9358d2c8a919" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293221 1034 "{58.9}^{∘}F" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534526 true] [17592186293221 1111 #uuid "182718cb-3d0e-5062-9eca-0f720915804e" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293223 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1089 "q-344695" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1100 "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1113 #uuid "50c4bf2d-5c40-5d7e-8775-995cfa67f088" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293222 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534526 true] [17592186293223 1000 #